GPIO, Interrupt & Character Device Driver Framework
Raspberry Pi 4 – Kernel ↔ Userspace GPIO Control
________________________________________
Overview
This project implements a custom Linux character device driver on Raspberry Pi 4 to control GPIO-based hardware (LEDs and push buttons) using interrupts.
The driver exposes GPIO control to user space via /dev/gpio_ctrl and supports:
•	Blocking read() on button events
•	poll() / select() support
•	ioctl() for configuration and status
•	Software debounce
•	Dynamic GPIO selection
The accompanying user-space application demonstrates how applications interact with the driver.
