Architecture
User App  ── open/read/write/ioctl/poll ──>  /dev/gpio_ctrl
                                                     |
                                                     v
                                      Custom Kernel Module
                                      - GPIO configuration
                                      - IRQ handlers for buttons
                                      - Debounce
                                      - Wait queues
•	Buttons generate hardware interrupts.
•	ISR increments a counter and wakes blocked readers.
•	read() blocks until a button press occurs.
•	ioctl() configures GPIO and reads state.
•	write() controls output GPIO (LED).
________________________________________
Functional Mapping
Feature	Implemented In Driver
Character device creation	alloc_chrdev_region, cdev_add, class_create
GPIO configuration	gpio_request, gpio_direction_*
Interrupt handling	request_irq, ISR
Debounce	jiffies-based filter
Blocking read	wait_event_interruptible
Poll/select	.poll + waitqueue
User-kernel copy	copy_to_user, copy_from_user
IOCTL interface	unlocked_ioctl
________________________________________

GPIO Wiring (Example)
•	LED:
•	GPIO (BCM) ──── LED Anode
•	                       LED Cathode ── GND
•	Button (Active-Low):
•	GPIO (BCM) ── Button ── VCC

The driver already configures two button GPIOs:
gpio_request(539, "BTN1");  // BCM27
gpio_request(540, "BTN2");  // BCM28 
________________________________________
Build & Run
Kernel Module:
make
sudo insmod gpio_ctrl.ko
dmesg | tail
ls -l /dev/gpio_ctrl
Unload:
sudo rmmod gpio_ctrl
User Application
gcc user_app.c -o user_app
sudo ./user_app
________________________________________
User Application Menu
1. Set GPIO
2. Set Direction
3. LED ON
4. LED OFF
5. Read GPIO
6. Blocking Read Button
7. Reset Counter
0. Exit
•	Set GPIO: Select which GPIO the driver controls
•	Set Direction: Configure as input/output
•	LED ON/OFF: Write to GPIO
•	Read GPIO: Read current GPIO value
•	Blocking Read Button: Wait until a button interrupt occurs
•	Reset Counter: Clear press count
